/-
P3 (DESIGN.md §9), invariant line G1 (INV-PLAN §4, epq1): **`RPos` kept by
every spec function of the kernel entry outside the configure path**, part 1
(spec side only, outside the `JAtZ` cone).

The family `PZK m := IK RPos m` is sg1's idle-pointer family SpecInvSgI1..I6
(ut7's NK family) renamed (`pz_` → `pz_`), with
* the primitive leaves replaced by SpecInvEqK's (`pz_setObject` for objects
  that are no SC, `pz_updateSchedContext` for updates keeping refills,
  period and refill max, retype / detype);
* the refill writers below the `RPos`-keeping level removed (refill pop /
  head / tail updates, `schedule_used`, the merge loops, `charge_entire_head_refill`,
  `handle_overrun`, `refill_new` / `refill_update`, the round-robin charges)
  and the writers SpecInvEqB proves by hand used as leaves
  (`refill_budget_check`, `refill_unblock_check`, `commit_time`,
  `sched_context_set_inactive`, `maybe_add_empty_tail`); `charge_budget` by
  hand in place (its round-robin branch resets a period-0 SC);
* the configure path removed: `invoke_sched_control_configure_flags` and its
  11 ancestors up to `fl4KernelEntrySyscall` (it needs decode and entry facts:
  SpecInvEqS).
Generated by proofs/scratch/epq1/tr.py (untracked). Parts 2-6: SpecInvEqG2..G6.
-/
